.TH ferry-peer-verify 1  Ferry "Ferry Manual"
.SH NAME
ferry\-peer\-verify \- Show the safety number shared with a trusted device, to compare it with the other device; `\-\-confirm` records that both match
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferry peer verify\fR [\fB\-\-confirm\fR] [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-\-unconfirm\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITARGET\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the safety number shared with a trusted device, to compare it with the other device; `\-\-confirm` records that both match
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-confirm\fR
The numbers are equal: mark the device as verified
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Interface language for this run (`en`, `pl`); overrides the saved setting
.TP
\fB\-\-unconfirm\fR
Remove the verified mark
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fITARGET\fR>
Alias or Node ID
